# An ALLOW-LIST, inverted: ignore everything, then un-ignore the handful of paths that are
# genuinely meant to land in somebody's home directory.
#
# WHY NOT A DENY-LIST: it was one, and it leaked. `debug-worker/` and `uninstall.sh` were
# added to the repo weeks apart, neither was on the list, and chezmoi was placing
# ~/debug-worker/wrangler.toml and ~/uninstall.sh into a stranger's home. A deny-list makes
# the DEFAULT "copy it into their home", and the default is what you get on the day nobody
# remembers to add a line.
#
# ⚠ THESE PATTERNS MATCH THE TARGET NAME, NOT THE SOURCE NAME. `dot_claude/**` matches
# nothing; the target is `.claude/**`. Writing the source name here silently places NOTHING
# — which is how the first version of this file dropped every skill and both settings files
# while looking correct.
*
!.claude
!.piy-shell.sh
!bin
!bin/piy
!.chezmoiscripts
!.chezmoiscripts/**
# The howto, placed ONCE (create_) as the root README of ~/piy-work — so it renders at
# http://127.0.0.1:29200/ — and never overwritten: ours on day one, theirs after. Nothing
# else under ~/piy-work, and nothing under ~/projects, is chezmoi's to see.
!piy-work
!piy-work/README.md

# The names from before 2026-10-02, ignored BY NAME. `*` above matches top-level names only
# (measured with `chezmoi managed`, 2026-10-02): `bin/mwk` and `.claude/skills/mwk-save` are
# not matched by it, so the allow-list does not cover anything nested. That matters here
# because a kit that arrived as a tarball is updated by untarring over itself, which deletes
# nothing — the old sources stay on disk, and without these lines the apply right after
# the retire script removed bin/mwk and the mwk-* skills would place them all again.
# There used to be a `!.claude/**` above; it went with this, because a `!` beats an ignore
# (measured) and it was un-ignoring the old skills. `*` never matched under .claude anyway.
bin/mwk
.claude/skills/mwk-*
.mwk-shell.sh
mwk-work
